# === dsh-deepartments patch: dsh-tool-fs-search path-not-found class (SEARCH_PATH_NOT_FOUND) ===
#
# WHAT THIS FIXES
#   glob/grep over a NON-EXISTENT path surfaced rg's raw stderr as a generic
#   SEARCH_FAILED ('rg: <path>: IO error for operation on <path>: No such file
#   or directory') — indistinguishable from a tool fault. This patch (a) adds a
#   path-cause PRE-CHECK in runRipgrep (a stat over the `-- <path>` target,
#   resolved against the session cwd; targets carrying glob metacharacters
#   skip it) that throws the clean `path not found: <path>` error BEFORE rg
#   spawns (fb-224/226/228/229), (b) classifies rg's own IO stderr
#   (`no such file or directory`) into the SAME SEARCH_PATH_NOT_FOUND branch as
#   a fallback, (c) tightens the SEARCH_INVALID_PATTERN wording to
#   `pattern rejected: <error line>` — the raw rg stderr body is no longer
#   embedded (q-i-107), and (d) documents the empty / path-not-found /
#   pattern-rejected distinction in the glob and grep tool descriptions
#   (MODO 3, VALLE 09-08 lane). The exit-1 empty result ('No files found' /
#   'No matches found') is UNTOUCHED: a missing path and a no-match search are
#   now distinguishable BY ERROR CODE (SEARCH_PATH_NOT_FOUND vs noMatches — the
#   fb-51 «un 0 no concluye no-existe» principle, by code).
#
# TARGET FILES
#   <npm-root>/@deepseek-ai/dsh/node_modules/@deepseek-ai/dsh-tool-fs-search/lib/index.js
#
# FINGERPRINTS (md5)  [anchor-applied rc.2 (the live base) -> patched]
#  index.js           c1ecd7ac43eaf7923af050eee8249673 -> 576e8e66b7a33e15fff58663c672272f
#
# ADDITIVE: applies ON TOP of dsh-tool-fs-search-anchor-literal-glob.patch
# (the base IS that patch's applied state, the live fingerprint c1ecd7ac…).
# No hunk re-applies an existing A-harness patch. The zone
# `a-harness-tool-fs-search-index` of scripts/zone-md5-manifest.json must be
# re-frozen to 576e8e66b7a33e15fff58663c672272f in the SAME change that
# applies this patch to the runtime.
